From: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: baldur: add the Gen5 GPR/APM prerequisites
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the three GPR/APM prerequisites the pinned tb323fu-linux series carries
and 7.2.6 does not have yet:

- drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c: install the service GPR callback before ->probe()
  and clear it when probe fails.  q6apm sends a synchronous command from its
  probe, whose response was previously dropped, delaying every boot by the
  5 s timeout.
- sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c/.h: send commands from the APM's own GPR
  service port (pkt->hdr.src_port = gdev->svc_id) and drop const from the
  packet argument in both the definition and the declaration.  The Kaanapali
  ADSP firmware only answers packets from the port the client is registered
  on.
- arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi: append <1024 8> to the ADSP GPR
  intents, keeping the existing <512 20> pair, because some ADSP responses
  exceed 512 bytes.

Rebased onto the actual 7.2.6 preimages from legacy patches 0075, 0076 and
0077 of the pinned tb323fu-linux tree at
11a25bf89b65fff48112a91a0b25bc247e7736d8 (Victor Fuentes).  The changes are
the original author's work; this rebase only re-derives the hunks and adds
no Signed-off-by.

AudioReach channel maps, suspend/resume and the Primary MI2S prepare path
are untouched.

---
 4 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
---

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
index ea7f83916d8d..39c3a6e6d1f0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -367,9 +367,11 @@
 	struct apr_driver *adrv = to_apr_driver(dev->driver);
 	int ret;
 
+	adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+
 	ret = adrv->probe(adev);
-	if (!ret)
-		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+	if (ret)
+		adev->svc.callback = NULL;
 
 	return ret;
 }
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
index 006e226d461e..57669db5666a 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -29,10 +29,12 @@
 
 static struct q6apm *g_apm;
 
-int q6apm_send_cmd_sync(struct q6apm *apm, const struct gpr_pkt *pkt,
+int q6apm_send_cmd_sync(struct q6apm *apm, struct gpr_pkt *pkt,
 			uint32_t rsp_opcode)
 {
 	gpr_device_t *gdev = apm->gdev;
+
+	pkt->hdr.src_port = gdev->svc_id;
 
 	return audioreach_send_cmd_sync(&gdev->dev, gdev, &apm->result, &apm->lock,
 					NULL, &apm->wait, pkt, rsp_opcode);
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.h b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.h
index 5cb51ca491dc..9092359ccf90 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.h
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.h
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@
 int q6apm_free_fragments(struct q6apm_graph *graph, unsigned int dir);
 int q6apm_unmap_memory_fixed_region(struct device *dev, unsigned int graph_id);
 /* Helpers */
-int q6apm_send_cmd_sync(struct q6apm *apm, const struct gpr_pkt *pkt,
+int q6apm_send_cmd_sync(struct q6apm *apm, struct gpr_pkt *pkt,
 			uint32_t rsp_opcode);
 
 /* Callback for graph specific */
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index dc51dee15230..a13e1afbc400 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -3004,7 +3004,7 @@
 					compatible = "qcom,gpr";
 					qcom,glink-channels = "adsp_apps";
 					qcom,domain = <GPR_DOMAIN_ID_ADSP>;
-					qcom,intents = <512 20>;
+					qcom,intents = <512 20>, <1024 8>;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
 
